node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
.env
coverage/
.packs/
# .smoke/ is NOT ignored: its src/ and package.json are the published-artifact
# test the release checklist tells you to run, and they were unreachable from a
# fresh clone while this line was here. .smoke/.gitignore already excludes the
# parts that must not be tracked — node_modules/ and package-lock.json.
*.tgz
.claude/
# CLAUDE.md is TRACKED. It is the project's own reference — the export list, the
# filter semantics, the wave and sprint history, the behaviour rules — and three
# sprints of tracked documents link to it by relative path, so ignoring it left
# every one of those links broken on GitHub and every edit invisible to a fresh
# clone. Decided in docs/sprints/sprint-2/05-repository-housekeeping.md.
#
# The self-presentation half moved to docs/marketing/, which stays ignored.
docs/marketing/
